{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1525117-wtf-2e-content-inquiry","id":1525117,"title":"WtF 2E Content Inquiry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-06T07:04:12-08:00","id":1525117,"title":"WtF 2E Content Inquiry","content":"Other than the 2 books below, are there any other books for settings in different cities, states or towns?<br /> <br /> CofD Silver Springs<br /> Splintered City Seattle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T07:51:02-08:00","id":1525118,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of location books, especially with bringing in Storyteller's Vault material like Silver Springs. 1e Vampire has City of the Damned New Orleans, 1e Werewolf has Hunting Grounds: The Rockies. 1e Werewolf also has Manitou Springs and Coyote Falls, both of which are pre-made adventures but could serve as a good starting point for a campaign, if I ever run a campaign I very well might set it in Manitou Springs. There's also a Chicago book (IIRC) that has stuff for vampire and werewolf. <br /> <br /> I know there's an L.A. Vampire book, I believe I've seen people discuss vampire books set in South America, but I don't think those books are in English. I'm not aware of any other location books for werewolf specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T09:36:54-08:00","id":1525122,"title":"","content":"Splintered City Seattle is a Demon book rather than a Werewolf one. I think it has just 1 page about the Uratha.<br /> <br /> In terms of 2e location books in general, there really aren't any official ones other than Splintered City. Each core book contains a handful of locations in chapter six - for example Werewolf features locations in Iraq, Northern Ireland, England, Michigan, Ohio, Australia, Japan, and Poland. The other books will all feature a similar variety of locations, but are unlikely to mention Werewolves.<br /> <br /> In terms of CofD Core books, Hurt Locker has a whole chapter on Tokyo, but doesn't mention any of the splats specifically. Nonetheless this could be a useful resource, since Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, and Beast all feature Tokyo in chapter six. You could also make use of the Contagion Chronicle and Global Outbreaks. These books are obviously focused on the Contagion Chronicle itself, but they do present 19 locations that you could mine for information.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind using or even playing in a historical setting, then you could take a look at the Dark Eras books. Dark Eras features seven times and places focused on Werewolves:<br /> <br /> Dark Eras<br /> The Sundered World - The Balkans circa 5000 BC<br /> The Wolf and the Raven - looks at several locations across Northern Europe impacted by Viking raids and expansion circa 700 AD<br /> The Bowery Dogs - New York in the 1970s<br /> <br /> Dark Eras Companion:<br /> Forsaken by Rome - Germania in the first century AD<br /> <br /> Dark Eras 2<br /> Hunger in the Black Land - Egypt 1806 BC<br /> The Great War - WWI the Western Front<br /> Fear and the Golden Promise of Tomorrow - The United States during WWII<br /> <br /> First edition is a goldmine for locations, and most of them can be used in 2e fairly seamlessly. The focus location for Werewolf in 1e was The Rockies, and it got a chapter in the Core Book and a then a whole book to itself - Hunting Ground: The Rockies. Werewolves got featured in 1e's big Vampire/Werewolf/Mage crossover book World of Darkness: Chicago, and they were the main focus in Shadows of the UK. Shadows of Mexico was a Vampire focused book, but it featured Werewolves quite heavily too.<br /> <br /> If you're willing to go beyond Werewolf, you've got City of the Damned: New Orleans and Requiem for Rome for Vampire, Boston Unveiled for Mage, Victorian Lost for Changeling, and lastly Mummy with Cursed Necropolis: DC and Cursed Necropolis: Rio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}